---
description: Git commit safety rules — prevents accidental file deletions in core submodule
alwaysApply: true
---

- In `core/`, never use `git add .`, `-A`, or `--all`; explicitly list every staged path.
- Before a `core/` commit run `git diff --cached --name-status` and allow only intended files, with no unexpected `D` or `M`.
- In root, use `git add .` only when the sole change is the intended `core` submodule ref; otherwise list paths.
- Never stage deletions you did not make; warn the user.
